\ wallet.fam — the wallet (docs/GUI_WALLET.md, phase 1), for wm's wallet
\ window: wm runs it as the session's user in the user's home, on pipes,
\ and it speaks the wallet's messages (docs/GUI_WALLET.md, The wallet's
\ messages): a JSON object a line each way, the first line wm's unlock
\ with the session's password, then each request answered by its op with
\ its id echoed.  It reads compact JSON (as JSON.stringify writes it).  It
\ ends when its input does.
\
\ Its records are a tree in the user's home, .wallet (mode 700), as
\ tabminer's wallet keeps an LMDB environment: "secret" the phrase's
\ entropy and its BIP39 seed, sealed under the password as tabminer seals
\ them (1, the rounds, a salt, a nonce, then ChaCha20-Poly1305 of the 80
\ bytes with the 33 before as associated data, the key the first 32
\ bytes of PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA512 of the password and "tabminer wallet" ||
\ salt); "address" the address counter (8 bytes; a new or restored
\ wallet's starts at a random 60-bit number: old addresses are never
\ used again, docs/PRIVACY.md); "scan" 1 while a restore waits for its
\ first scan.  The password is the session's: wm's, as typed at logging
\ in.
\
\ The node is its API on 127.0.0.1:3738, without the token (reads are
\ open).  The wallet's outputs are found by reading the whole unspent set
\ (/v1/outputs, a thousand a request) and checking each memo's tag: one
\ of this wallet's has its key derived and its commitment checked before
\ it is recorded; one once in the set and no longer there was spent.  The
\ set is read again whenever the tip moves (the node asked every 4 s
\ while no request comes), and the tip told (an event); a reorganization
\ needs nothing more.  Reading block by block can come later, when the
\ set is large.
\
\ Built so far (step 2 of 4): unlock, create, restore, phrase, receive,
\ overview, scan; the tip told.  The rest are refused as not yet built.
\ uses: crypto/sha512.fam crypto/sha256.fam crypto/bip39.fam crypto/chacha.fam crypto/keccak.fam crypto/dilithium.fam
\ uses: node/arith.fam node/poseidon2.fam node/difficulty.fam node/pow.fam node/state.fam node/xmss.fam node/xsign.fam node/wkeys.fam node/wslate.fam
\ memory: 4096
: ibuf variable ;  : icnt variable ;  : obuf variable ;  : opos variable ;
: idb variable ;  : opb variable ;  : unl variable ;  : jr variable ;
: lp variable ;  : le variable ;

\ jo ( s -- )  s added to the line being written, each ' a double quote
\ (fam's strings hold none); jraw ( s -- ) s as it is; jend the line
\ written, a newline after it.
: jo
opos @ swap
begin dup c@ ?dup while dup 27 lit = if drop 22 lit then 2 lit pick c! swap 1 lit + swap 1 lit + repeat
drop opos ! ;
: jraw  opos @ swap scpy opos ! ;
: jend  A lit opos @ c!  1 lit obuf @ opos @ obuf @ - 1 lit + write drop  obuf @ opos ! ;

\ jfm ( a key -- flag )  key (' for a double quote) at a.
\ jfind ( line key -- a | 0 )  just past the first key in the line.
: jfm
begin dup c@ if over c@ over c@ dup 27 lit = if drop 22 lit then = else 0 lit then while
	1 lit + swap 1 lit + swap
repeat
nip c@ 0= ;
: jfind
0 lit jr !  swap
begin dup c@ jr @ 0= and while
	2dup swap jfm if dup 2 lit pick strlen + jr ! then
	1 lit +
repeat 2drop jr @ ;

\ getid ( line -- )  the request's id at idb as sent (up to a comma or a
\ brace), or null; getop ( line -- ) its op at opb (31 bytes at most), or
\ empty.
: getid
idb @ swap "'id':" jfind ?dup if
	begin dup c@ dup 2C lit <> over 7D lit <> and and while dup c@ 2 lit pick c! swap 1 lit + swap 1 lit + repeat drop
else "null" scpy then
0 lit swap c! ;
: getop
opb @ swap "'op':'" jfind ?dup if
	begin dup c@ dup 22 lit <> and  2 lit pick opb @ - 1F lit u< and while
		dup c@ 2 lit pick c! swap 1 lit + swap 1 lit + repeat drop
then
0 lit swap c! ;

\ jstr ( line key dst max -- flag )  the string after key (as "'words':'")
\ at dst, its escapes undone (\" \\ \/ \n \t \r \b \f, \u00XX), NUL-ended,
\ max - 1 bytes at most; whether the key was there and the string fit.
: jsd variable ;  : jsm variable ;  : jsok variable ;
: jhx  dup 3A lit u< if 30 lit - else 20 lit or 57 lit - then F lit and ;   \ ( c -- n )
: jsput  jsm @ 1 lit u> if jsd @ c!  jsd @ 1 lit + jsd !  jsm @ 1 lit - jsm ! else drop 0 lit jsok ! then ;
: jstr
jsm !  jsd !  jfind dup jsok !
dup if
	begin dup c@ dup 22 lit <> and while
		dup c@ 5C lit = if
			1 lit +  dup c@
			dup 6E lit = if drop A lit else dup 74 lit = if drop 9 lit else dup 72 lit = if drop D lit else
			dup 62 lit = if drop 8 lit else dup 66 lit = if drop C lit else
			dup 75 lit = if drop dup 3 lit + c@ jhx 4 lit lshift over 4 lit + c@ jhx or  swap 4 lit + swap then
			then then then then then
			jsput
		else dup c@ jsput then
		1 lit +
	repeat
	c@ 0= if 0 lit jsok ! then
else drop then
0 lit jsd @ c!  jsok @ 0= 0= ;

\ jok  an answer begun: its id, ok; jerr ( s -- ) an error answered.
: jok  "{'id':" jo idb @ jraw ",'ok':true" jo ;
: jerr  "{'id':" jo idb @ jraw ",'ok':false,'error':'" jo jo "'}" jo jend ;
: op?  opb @ swap streq ;                                    \ ( s -- flag )

\ ── The records ──

: wfd variable ;  : pw variable ;  : have variable ;  : rec variable ;  : plain variable ;  : wkey variable ;
: salt2 variable ;  : wphr variable ;  : wseed variable ;  : wtmp variable ;  : wcnt variable ;
: wpk variable ;  : wsk variable ;  : waddr variable ;  : wf1 variable ;  : wf2 variable ;
:M ROUNDS 4E20 lit ;                         \ the password's PBKDF2 rounds (fam's: about 1.4 s)

\ wrand ( dst n -- )  n bytes from /dev/random.
: wrf variable ;  : wrd variable ;  : wrn variable ;
: wrand
wrn !  wrd !  "/dev/random" 0 lit open wrf !
begin wrn @ while
	wrf @ wrd @ wrn @ read  dup 0 lit > if dup wrd @ + wrd !  wrn @ swap - wrn ! else drop then
repeat
wrf @ close drop ;
\ wopen ( create? -- flag )  the tree open (made, mode 700, if asked).
: wopen
wfd @ 0< 0= if drop -1 lit else
	".wallet" TREE 2 lit or rot if CREATE or then open dup wfd !
	0< 0= dup if ".wallet" 1C0 lit chmod drop then
then ;
\ wget ( key buf n -- vlen | <0 )  one record, read in a snapshot.
\ wbeg  the writer's transaction begun; wset ( key value n -- ) a record
\ in it; wend ( -- ok ) it committed, all its records or none.
: wgk variable ;  : wtx variable ;
: wget  wf2 !  wf1 !  wgk !  wfd @ 0 lit txbegin  dup wgk @ dup strlen wf1 @ wf2 @ txget  swap txabort drop ;
: wbeg  wfd @ 1 lit txbegin wtx ! ;
: wset  wf2 !  wf1 !  wgk !  wtx @ wgk @ dup strlen wf1 @ wf2 @ txput drop ;
: wend  wtx @ txcommit 0= ;

\ wkdf ( pw rec -- )  wkey (32 bytes) = PBKDF2 of the password with the
\ record's rounds and "tabminer wallet" || its salt (16 bytes at 5).
: wkr variable ;  : wkp variable ;
: wkdf
wkr !  wkp !
salt2 @ "tabminer wallet" scpy  wkr @ 5 lit + swap 10 lit bcopy
wkp @ dup strlen salt2 @ 1F lit wkr @ 1 lit + le@ wtmp @ 40 lit pbkdf512
wtmp @ wkey @ 20 lit bcopy ;
\ wseal  rec (129 bytes) = plain (the entropy, the seed) sealed under pw:
\ 1, the rounds, a salt (16), a nonce (12), the 96 sealed bytes.
: wseal
1 lit rec @ c!  ROUNDS rec @ 1 lit + wkle!  rec @ 5 lit + 10 lit wrand  rec @ 15 lit + C lit wrand
pw @ rec @ wkdf
wkey @ rec @ 15 lit + rec @ 21 lit plain @ 50 lit rec @ 21 lit + aeseal ;
\ wunseal ( pw -- flag )  plain from the record, if the password is its.
: wunseal
"secret" rec @ 100 lit wget 81 lit =  rec @ c@ 1 lit = and
dup if
	drop rec @ wkdf
	wkey @ rec @ 15 lit + rec @ 21 lit rec @ 21 lit + 50 lit plain @ aeopen
else nip then ;

\ The address: the Dilithium key of the address counter, its id in text.
: waok variable ;
: waddr!
waok @ 0= if
	wcnt @ wtmp @ wkidsd  wtmp @ wpk @ wsk @ dilkey  wpk @ wtmp @ wkid  wtmp @ waddr @ wkaddr
	1 lit waok !
then ;
\ wrcnt  a new counter: 60 random bits.
: wrcnt
wcnt @ 8 lit wrand
wcnt @ @ 4 lit rshift  wcnt @ 4 lit + @ 1C lit lshift or
wcnt @ 4 lit + @ 4 lit rshift  wcnt @ 4 lit + !  wcnt @ ! ;
\ wmake ( scan? -- ok )  a wallet made from plain: the tree, its records
\ in one transaction; the master.
: wmake
1 lit wopen if
	wrcnt  wseal  0 lit waok !
	wbeg
	"secret" rec @ 81 lit wset
	1 lit wtmp @ c!  "format" wtmp @ 1 lit wset
	"address" wcnt @ 8 lit wset
	if 1 lit wtmp @ c!  "scan" wtmp @ 1 lit wset then
	wend
	dup if plain @ 10 lit + wkmast  1 lit have ! then
else drop 0 lit then ;
\ wload  an opened wallet's records: the counter, the master.
: wload  "address" wcnt @ 8 lit wget drop  plain @ 10 lit + wkmast  1 lit have !  0 lit waok ! ;

\ ── The node: its API (docs/NODE.md, The API), on 127.0.0.1:3738 ──

: hbuf variable ;  : hreq variable ;  : hs variable ;  : hn variable ;  : hres variable ;  : hpath variable ;
:M HMAX 40000 lit ;
: wcrlf  D lit over c!  1 lit +  A lit over c!  1 lit + ;      \ ( a -- a' )
\ hbody  hres = the body of the answer in hbuf (after the blank line).
: hbody
hn @ 3 lit - 0 lit do
	hres @ 0= if
		hbuf @ i + c@ D lit =  hbuf @ i + 1 lit + c@ A lit = and  hbuf @ i + 2 lit + c@ D lit = and
		if hbuf @ i + 4 lit + hres ! then
	then
loop ;
\ Numbers of 64 bits, as nlo and dhi.
: nlo variable ;  : nhi variable ;  : ndc variable ;  : nla variable ;  : nlb variable ;  : nca variable ;  : ncb variable ;
: nls variable ;  : nc1 variable ;  : nc2 variable ;  : nq0 variable ;  : nq1 variable ;  : nq2 variable ;  : nq3 variable ;
: ndn variable ;  : ntmp variable ;
\ d10+ ( d -- )  dlo:dhi times ten, plus d.
: d10+
ndc !
nlo @ 3 lit lshift nla !  nlo @ 1D lit rshift nca !
nlo @ 1 lit lshift nlb !  nlo @ 1F lit rshift ncb !
nla @ nlb @ + nls !  nls @ nla @ u< 1 lit and nc1 !
nls @ ndc @ + dup nls @ u< 1 lit and nc2 !  nlo !
nhi @ A lit * nca @ + ncb @ + nc1 @ + nc2 @ + nhi ! ;
\ jnum ( a -- a' )  the decimal digits at a into dlo:dhi; a' past them.
: jnum  0 lit nlo !  0 lit nhi !  begin dup c@ 30 lit - A lit u< while dup c@ 30 lit - d10+ 1 lit + repeat ;
\ dq16 ( r limb -- r' q )  one 16-bit step of dividing by ten.
: dq16  swap 10 lit lshift or  dup A lit /  tuck A lit * -  swap ;
\ du10 ( -- r )  dlo:dhi divided by ten; the remainder.
: du10
0 lit  nhi @ 10 lit rshift dq16 nq3 !  nhi @ FFFF lit and dq16 nq2 !
nlo @ 10 lit rshift dq16 nq1 !  nlo @ FFFF lit and dq16 nq0 !
nq3 @ 10 lit lshift nq2 @ or nhi !  nq1 @ 10 lit lshift nq0 @ or nlo ! ;
\ ddig ( lo hi n -- )  its decimal digits at dtmp, least first, n at
\ least; how many in dn.
: ddig
ndc !  nhi !  nlo !  0 lit ndn !
begin du10 30 lit + ntmp @ ndn @ + c!  ndn @ 1 lit + ndn !  nlo @ nhi @ or 0= ndn @ ndc @ u< 0= and until ;
\ jc ( c -- )  a byte added to the line being written.
: jc  opos @ c!  opos @ 1 lit + opos ! ;
\ wamt ( lo hi -- )  an amount in coins, its ten decimals, written.
: wamt
B lit ddig
ndn @ 0 lit do ntmp @ ndn @ 1 lit - i - + c@ jc  ndn @ 1 lit - i - A lit = if 2E lit jc then loop ;
\ wdec ( lo hi -- )  a number in decimal, written.
: wdec  1 lit ddig  ndn @ 0 lit do ntmp @ ndn @ 1 lit - i - + c@ jc loop ;
\ dstr ( lo hi dst -- dst' )  the same into a string.
: dstr  -rot 1 lit ddig  ndn @ 0 lit do ntmp @ ndn @ 1 lit - i - + c@ over c!  1 lit + loop  0 lit over c! ;
\ jhexb ( a dst n -- )  n bytes from 2n hex digits at a.
: jhexb  0 lit do over i 1 lit lshift + c@ jhx 4 lit lshift  2 lit pick i 1 lit lshift + 1 lit + c@ jhx or  over i + c! loop 2drop ;

\ hask ( method path body n -- body | 0 )  a request (a body of n bytes
\ unless n is 0) answered: its body, NUL-ended; the status in hcode (0:
\ the node not reached).
: hcode variable ;  : hmeth variable ;  : hbd variable ;  : hbn variable ;
: hask
hbn !  hbd !  hpath !  hmeth !  0 lit hn !  0 lit hres !  0 lit hcode !
2 lit socket hs !
hs @ 2 lit 7F000001 lit E9A lit net 0< 0= if
	hreq @ hmeth @ scpy " " scpy hpath @ scpy " HTTP/1.0" scpy wcrlf
	hbn @ if "Content-Length: " scpy hbn @ 0 lit rot dstr wcrlf then
	wcrlf hreq @ -
	hs @ hreq @ rot write drop
	hbn @ if hs @ hbd @ hbn @ write drop then
	begin hs @ hbuf @ hn @ + HMAX 1 lit - hn @ - read  dup 0 lit > while hn @ + hn ! repeat drop
	0 lit hbuf @ hn @ + c!
	hn @ C lit u< 0= if
		hbuf @ 9 lit + c@ 30 lit - 64 lit *  hbuf @ A lit + c@ 30 lit - A lit * +  hbuf @ B lit + c@ 30 lit - + hcode !
		hbody
	then
then
hs @ close drop  hres @ ;
\ hget ( path -- body | 0 )  a GET answered 200: its body.
: hget  "GET" swap 0 lit 0 lit hask  hcode @ C8 lit = and ;

\ ── The outputs: records "o" || commitment (33 bytes), 48 bytes each ──
\ +0 the nonce (4 canonical words), +10 the amount, +18 the position (8;
\ all ones: not yet in the set), +20 the height it was made at, +24 the
\ state (0 unspent, 1 reserved, 2 spent), +25 the first leaf, +26 leaves
\ used, +27 recovered (found by a scan, not made here: its leaves the
\ second half's, as tabminer's), +28 the scan that last saw it.

: okey variable ;  : orec variable ;  : wkl variable ;  : sgen variable ;
: ecom variable ;  : emem variable ;  : eamt variable ;  : epos variable ;  : eh variable ;  : ecb variable ;
: xk variable ;  : wxpk variable ;  : kseed variable ;  : scur variable ;  : scnt variable ;  : sfrom variable ;
: ltip variable ;  : ntip variable ;  : lh variable ;  : nodeok variable ;  : okn variable ;  : ppath variable ;
\ wgetk ( key klen buf n -- vlen )  in the writer's transaction.
: wgetk  wf2 !  wf1 !  wkl !  wgk !  wtx @ wgk @ wkl @ wf1 @ wf2 @ txget ;
: wsetk  wf2 !  wf1 !  wkl !  wgk !  wtx @ wgk @ wkl @ wf1 @ wf2 @ txput drop ;
\ wone  one output of the set (ecom, emem, eamt, epos, eh) checked: a
\ known one's position and scan noted; an unknown one with this wallet's
\ tag, its key derived and its commitment checked, recorded as found.
: wone
6F lit okey @ c!  ecom @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk 30 lit = if
	epos @ orec @ 18 lit + 8 lit bcopy  eh @ @ orec @ 20 lit + !  sgen @ orec @ 28 lit + !
	okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
else
	emem @ wkopen if
		kseed @ wkkey  kseed @ 4 lit xk @ xkgen  xk @ wxpk @ xkpub
		wxpk @ eamt @ ecb @ wkcom  ecb @ ecb @ 20 lit + wkcan
		ecb @ 20 lit + ecom @ 20 lit wssame if
			orec @ 30 lit 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop drop
			emem @ orec @ 10 lit bcopy  eamt @ orec @ 10 lit + 8 lit bcopy  epos @ orec @ 18 lit + 8 lit bcopy
			eh @ @ orec @ 20 lit + !  wtmp @ 1 lit wrand  wtmp @ c@ 7 lit and orec @ 25 lit + c!
			1 lit orec @ 27 lit + c!  sgen @ orec @ 28 lit + !
			okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
		then
	then
then ;
\ wpage ( -- n )  a page of the set from sfrom (8 bytes) checked: how many.
: wpage
0 lit scnt !
ppath @ "/v1/outputs?from=" scpy  sfrom @ @ sfrom @ 4 lit + @ rot dstr "&count=1000" scpy drop
ppath @ hget dup scur !
if
	wbeg
	begin scur @ "'position':" jfind ?dup while
		jnum scur !  nlo @ epos @ !  nhi @ epos @ 4 lit + !
		scur @ "'commitment':'" jfind ecom @ 20 lit jhexb
		scur @ "'memo':'" jfind emem @ 14 lit jhexb
		scur @ "'amount':" jfind jnum drop  nlo @ eamt @ !  nhi @ eamt @ 4 lit + !
		scur @ "'height':" jfind jnum scur !  nlo @ eh @ !
		wone  scnt @ 1 lit + scnt !
		\ the next page from the position after this one
		epos @ @ 1 lit + dup sfrom @ !  0= if epos @ 4 lit + @ 1 lit + else epos @ 4 lit + @ then sfrom @ 4 lit + !
	repeat
	wend drop
then
scnt @ ;
\ wspent  the outputs once in the set and not seen by this scan: spent.
: wspent
wbeg
6F lit okey @ c!  1 lit
begin wtx @ okey @ rot okn @ txnext dup 21 lit = if okn @ c@ 6F lit = else 0 lit then while
	drop  okn @ okey @ 21 lit bcopy
	okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop
	orec @ 1C lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit <>  orec @ 28 lit + @ sgen @ <> and  orec @ 24 lit + c@ 2 lit <> and if
		2 lit orec @ 24 lit + c!  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
	then
	21 lit
repeat drop
wend drop ;
\ wscan ( -- ok )  the whole unspent set read through the node.
: wscan
"gen" wtmp @ 4 lit wget 4 lit = if wtmp @ @ else 0 lit then 1 lit + sgen !
0 lit sfrom @ !  0 lit sfrom @ 4 lit + !  1 lit nodeok !
begin wpage dup 0= if hres @ 0= if 0 lit nodeok ! then then 3E8 lit u< until
nodeok @ if
	wspent
	wbeg  sgen @ wtmp @ !  "gen" wtmp @ 4 lit wset  0 lit wtmp @ c!  "scan" wtmp @ 1 lit wset  wend drop
then
nodeok @ ;
\ wtick  the node asked for its tip; when it moved, the set scanned again
\ and the tip told (an event).
: wtick
have @ if
	"/v1/status" hget ?dup if
		dup "'height':" jfind jnum drop nlo @ lh !
		"'tip':'" jfind ntip @ 40 lit bcopy  0 lit ntip @ 40 lit + c!
		ntip @ ltip @ streq 0= if
			wscan if
				ltip @ ntip @ scpy drop
				"{'event':'tip','height':" jo lh @ 0 lit wdec ",'hash':'" jo ltip @ jraw "'}" jo jend
			then
		then
	else 0 lit nodeok ! then
then ;
: wsum.  dup @ swap 4 lit + @ wamt ;                      \ ( acc -- )  written

: nowal  "no wallet yet: create or restore one" jerr ;

\ ── Payments (step 3): files, amounts, new outputs ──

: fbuf variable ;  : fn variable ;  : ffd variable ;
:M FMAX 8000 lit ;
\ fread ( path -- n | -1 )  a file of FMAX bytes at most into fbuf.
: fread
0 lit open dup ffd !  0< if FFFFFFFF lit else
	0 lit fn !
	begin ffd @ fbuf @ fn @ + FMAX fn @ - read  dup 0 lit > fn @ FMAX u< and while fn @ + fn ! repeat drop
	ffd @ close drop  fn @
then ;
\ fwrite ( path a n -- ok )  a file written whole (made, or emptied).
: fwa variable ;  : fwn variable ;
: fwrite
fwn !  fwa !  1 lit CREATE or TRUNC or open dup ffd !
0< if 0 lit else ffd @ fwa @ fwn @ write fwn @ =  ffd @ close drop then ;

\ Amounts, 8 bytes at an address.
: aa variable ;  : ab variable ;  : ad variable ;
\ a8add ( a b dst -- )  dst = a + b; a8sub ( a b dst -- ) dst = a - b.
: a8add
ad !  ab !  aa !
aa @ @ ab @ @ +  dup aa @ @ u< 1 lit and  aa @ 4 lit + @ +  ab @ 4 lit + @ +
ad @ 4 lit + !  ad @ ! ;
: a8sub
ad !  ab !  aa !
aa @ @ ab @ @ -  aa @ @ ab @ @ u< 1 lit and  aa @ 4 lit + @ ab @ 4 lit + @ - swap -
ad @ 4 lit + !  ad @ ! ;
\ a8lt ( a b -- flag )  a below b.
: a8lt
ab !  aa !
aa @ 4 lit + @ ab @ 4 lit + @ = if aa @ @ ab @ @ u< else aa @ 4 lit + @ ab @ 4 lit + @ u< then ;
\ a8set ( lo hi dst -- )
: a8set  ad !  ad @ 4 lit + !  ad @ ! ;

\ jcoins ( s dst -- ok )  coins as text (up to ten decimals) into base
\ units at dst.
: jcs variable ;  : jcd variable ;  : jcn variable ;  : jcf variable ;  : jck variable ;
: jcs+  jcs @ 1 lit + jcs ! ;
: jdig?  jcs @ c@ 30 lit - A lit u< ;
: jcoins
jcd !  jcs !  0 lit nlo !  0 lit nhi !  0 lit jcn !  0 lit jcf !  -1 lit jck !
begin jdig? while jcs @ c@ 30 lit - d10+ jcs+ jcn @ 1 lit + jcn ! repeat
jcs @ c@ 2E lit = if
	jcs+
	begin jdig? while jcs @ c@ 30 lit - d10+ jcs+ jcn @ 1 lit + jcn !  jcf @ 1 lit + jcf ! repeat
then
jcf @ A lit u> if 0 lit jck ! then
jcs @ c@ if 0 lit jck ! then
jcn @ 0= if 0 lit jck ! then
jck @ if A lit jcf @ - ?dup if 0 lit do 0 lit d10+ loop then then
nlo @ nhi @ jcd @ a8set  jck @ ;

\ wrfp ( a -- )  a random field element (below p) at a.
: wrfp
begin wtmp @ 4 lit wrand  wtmp @ @ 7FFFFFFF lit and  dup 78000001 lit u< 0= while drop repeat
swap ! ;
\ wnew ( amt kind -- )  a new output of this wallet's, in the writer's
\ transaction: a random nonce, its key, its memo; onew the output (60
\ bytes), ecom its commitment; recorded as not yet in the set (kind: 0
\ found, 1 received by an answer, 2 change).
: wna variable ;  : wnk variable ;  : nb variable ;  : wmb variable ;  : onew variable ;
: wnew
wnk !  wna !
4 lit 0 lit do nb @ i 2 lit lshift + wrfp loop
nb @ wknon  kseed @ wkkey  kseed @ 4 lit xk @ xkgen  xk @ wxpk @ xkpub  wmb @ wkmemo
wxpk @ wna @ wmb @ onew @ wsmkout
wxpk @ wna @ ecb @ wkcom  ecb @ ecom @ wkcan
orec @ 30 lit 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop drop
nb @ orec @ 10 lit bcopy  wna @ orec @ 10 lit + 8 lit bcopy
FFFFFFFF lit orec @ 18 lit + !  FFFFFFFF lit orec @ 1C lit + !  wnk @ orec @ 29 lit + c!
6F lit okey @ c!  ecom @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk ;

\ wrget ( key klen buf n -- vlen )  one record, read in a snapshot.
: wrget  wf2 !  wf1 !  wkl !  wgk !  wfd @ 0 lit txbegin  dup wgk @ wkl @ wf1 @ wf2 @ txget  swap txabort drop ;
\ jhex ( a n -- )  n bytes written in hex.
: jhd  F lit and dup A lit u< if 30 lit + else 57 lit + then jc ;
: jhex  ?dup if 0 lit do dup i + c@ dup 4 lit rshift jhd jhd loop then drop ;
: a8.  dup @ swap 4 lit + @ wamt ;                     \ ( a -- )  in coins, written
: fpath variable ;  : fout variable ;  : fpn variable ;

\ oanswer ( line -- )  a payer's slate (stage 1) answered: this wallet's
\ output added and recorded, its receipt signed, the answer written to
\ the file's name and ".received" (as tabminer's receive).
: oanswer
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
"'slate':'" fpath @ 100 lit jstr 0= if "no slate file" jerr else
fpath @ fread fpn !  fpn @ 0< if "the slate file cannot be read" jerr else
fbuf @ fpn @ wsparse 0= if "not a slate" jerr else
wsstg @ 1 lit <> if "not a slate to answer" jerr else
wsnout @ wschg @ <> if "the slate is answered already" jerr else
	waddr!
	wbeg  wsa @ 49 lit + 1 lit wnew  wend
	if
		onew @ wsk @ wpk @ wsans fpn !
		fout @ fpath @ scpy ".received" scpy drop
		fout @ wsbuf @ fpn @ fwrite if
			jok ",'slate':'" jo fout @ jraw "','amount':'" jo wsa @ 49 lit + a8. "'}" jo jend
		else "the answer cannot be written" jerr then
	else "the wallet could not be written" jerr then
then then then then then then ;

\ The fees: /v1/fees's rates (a byte) for a block, an hour, a day, and
\ economy.
: frk variable ;
\ frate ( body speed -- rate )  a speed's rate (10, the floor, if unknown).
: frate
frk @ "'" scpy swap scpy "':{'rate':" scpy drop
frk @ jfind ?dup if jnum drop nlo @ else A lit then ;
: ofees
"/v1/fees" hget ?dup 0= if "the node is not reached" jerr else
	jok ",'speeds':[{'speed':'block','rate':" jo dup "block" frate 0 lit wdec
	",'wait':600},{'speed':'hour','rate':" jo dup "hour" frate 0 lit wdec
	",'wait':3600},{'speed':'day','rate':" jo dup "day" frate 0 lit wdec
	",'wait':86400},{'speed':'economy','rate':" jo "economy" frate 0 lit wdec ",'wait':604800}]}" jo jend
then ;

\ The coins to spend: sel, entries of 40 bytes (the commitment, the
\ amount), largest first; nsel of them.
: sel variable ;  : nsel variable ;  : se variable ;  : sk variable ;
: selent  6 lit lshift sel @ + ;                         \ ( i -- a )
\ wsels  the confirmed unspent outputs gathered (64 at most), sorted.
: wsels
0 lit nsel !
wfd @ 0 lit txbegin wtx !
6F lit okey @ c!  1 lit
begin wtx @ okey @ rot okn @ txnext dup 21 lit = if okn @ c@ 6F lit = else 0 lit then while
	drop  okn @ okey @ 21 lit bcopy
	okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop
	orec @ 24 lit + c@ 0=  orec @ 1C lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit <> and  nsel @ 40 lit u< and if
		okey @ 1 lit + nsel @ selent 20 lit bcopy  orec @ 10 lit + nsel @ selent 20 lit + 8 lit bcopy
		nsel @ 1 lit + nsel !
	then
	21 lit
repeat drop
wtx @ txabort drop
\ largest first: each place takes the largest of those after it
nsel @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	i se !
	nsel @ i do  se @ selent 20 lit + i selent 20 lit + a8lt if i se ! then  loop
	se @ i <> if
		i selent wtmp @ 40 lit bcopy  se @ selent i selent 40 lit bcopy  wtmp @ se @ selent 40 lit bcopy
	then
loop then ;

\ The payment's numbers, 8 bytes each: the amount, the fee, what is
\ needed, what the coins picked hold, the change; the rate, the inputs.
: samt variable ;  : sfee variable ;  : sneed variable ;  : stot variable ;  : schg variable ;
: srate variable ;  : snin variable ;  : spick variable ;  : sdone variable ;  : sdust variable ;
: pend variable ;  : sid variable ;  : ssec variable ;  : ssnd variable ;  : pkb variable ;
\ spick! ( -- )  coins taken largest first until they hold sneed: spick of
\ them, stot their sum.
: spick!
0 lit spick !  0 lit stot @ !  0 lit stot @ 4 lit + !
begin spick @ nsel @ u<  stot @ sneed @ a8lt and while
	stot @ spick @ selent 20 lit + stot @ a8add  spick @ 1 lit + spick !
repeat ;
\ wfee  sfee = the rate times a payment's size with snin inputs (16 +
\ 2,377 each + two outputs of 60), sneed = samt + sfee.
: wfee  snin @ 949 lit * 88 lit +  srate @ *  0 lit sfee @ a8set  samt @ sfee @ sneed @ a8add ;
\ wpkof ( commitment dst -- )  an output's public key (49 bytes): its key
\ derived from its record's nonce.
: wpkof
swap 6F lit okey @ c!  okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wrget drop
orec @ wknon  kseed @ wkkey  kseed @ 4 lit xk @ xkgen  xk @ swap xkpub ;
\ osend ( line -- )  a payment begun by file: coins picked, change made,
\ the coins reserved and the payment recorded in one transaction, the
\ stage-1 slate written for the recipient.  The sender is unnamed (the
\ hash of a secret kept, docs/PRIVACY.md).
: osend
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
dup "'amount':'" wtmp @ 40 lit jstr  wtmp @ samt @ jcoins and 0= if drop "not an amount" jerr else
samt @ sdust @ a8lt if drop "the amount is below the dust limit" jerr else
dup "'slate':'" fpath @ 100 lit jstr 0= if drop "no slate file" jerr else
"'speed':'" wtmp @ 20 lit jstr drop
"/v1/fees" hget ?dup if wtmp @ frate else A lit then srate !
wsels
1 lit snin !  0 lit sdone !
begin sdone @ 0= while
	wfee spick!
	stot @ sneed @ a8lt if 2 lit sdone ! else
	spick @ snin @ u> if spick @ snin ! else 1 lit sdone ! then then
repeat
sdone @ 2 lit = if "not enough confirmed coins" jerr else
	\ the change, or below the dust limit, the fee's
	stot @ sneed @ schg @ a8sub
	schg @ sdust @ a8lt if sfee @ schg @ sfee @ a8add  0 lit 0 lit schg @ a8set then
	sid @ 20 lit wrand  ssec @ 20 lit wrand  ssec @ wsd @ wstag  wsd @ ssnd @ wkcan
	\ the record: inputs, change, amount, fee, sender, secret, change's
	\ commitment, the inputs' commitments
	pend @ 78 lit 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop drop
	spick @ pend @ !  samt @ pend @ 8 lit + 8 lit bcopy  sfee @ pend @ 10 lit + 8 lit bcopy
	ssnd @ pend @ 18 lit + 20 lit bcopy  ssec @ pend @ 38 lit + 20 lit bcopy
	spick @ 0 lit do i selent pend @ 78 lit + i 5 lit lshift + 20 lit bcopy loop
	wbeg
	schg @ @ schg @ 4 lit + @ or if
		schg @ 2 lit wnew  1 lit pend @ 4 lit + !  ecom @ pend @ 58 lit + 20 lit bcopy
	then
	spick @ 0 lit do
		6F lit okey @ c!  i selent okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
		okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop  1 lit orec @ 24 lit + c!  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
	loop
	73 lit okey @ c!  sid @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  okey @ 21 lit pend @ 78 lit spick @ 5 lit lshift + wsetk
	wend if
		\ the slate: its inputs' keys derived, its change
		sid @ ssnd @ samt @ sfee @ wsbeg
		spick @ 0 lit do  i selent pkb @ wpkof  pkb @ i selent 20 lit + wsaddin  loop
		pend @ 4 lit + @ if onew @ wsaddout then
		pend @ 4 lit + @ wsfix fpn !
		fpath @ wsbuf @ fpn @ fwrite if
			jok ",'slate':'" jo fpath @ jraw "','fee':'" jo sfee @ a8. "'}" jo jend
		else "the slate cannot be written" jerr then
	else "the wallet could not be written" jerr then
then
then then then then ;

\ ofinal ( line -- )  the recipient's answer finalized: tabminer's checks
\ against the payment's record (wsfin); each input's next leaf recorded as
\ used, committed, before any signature is made; the transaction signed
\ and sent to the node; accepted, the inputs spent, the payment recorded.
: fkeys variable ;  : fka variable ;  : flv variable ;  : fps variable ;  : pins variable ;  : fchg variable ;
: fcode variable ;  : fnin variable ;  : ftx variable ;  : fbad variable ;
\ wfmsg ( code -- )  wsfin's refusal answered.
: wfmsg
dup 1 lit = if drop "not an answered slate" else dup 2 lit = if drop "its inputs changed" else
dup 3 lit = if drop "no output for the recipient" else dup 4 lit = if drop "its amount or fee changed" else
dup 5 lit = if drop "its amounts do not balance" else dup 6 lit = if drop "its change changed" else
dup 7 lit = if drop "an output is zero or below the dust limit" else dup 8 lit = if drop "it is too large" else
9 lit = if "not one output for the recipient" else "the receipt does not hold" then
then then then then then then then then jerr ;
: ofinal
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
"'slate':'" fpath @ 100 lit jstr 0= if "no slate file" jerr else
fpath @ fread fpn !  fpn @ 0< if "the slate file cannot be read" jerr else
fbuf @ fpn @ wsparse 0= if "not a slate" jerr else
73 lit okey @ c!  wsa @ 8 lit + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
okey @ 21 lit pend @ 878 lit wrget 0< if "not a payment this wallet began" jerr else
	pend @ @ fnin !  0 lit fbad !
	\ the inputs: keys, public keys and amounts, leaves, positions
	fnin @ 0 lit do
		6F lit okey @ c!  pend @ 78 lit + i 5 lit lshift + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
		okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wrget drop
		orec @ wknon  kseed @ wkkey  fkeys @ i 440 lit * + dup fka @ i 2 lit lshift + !
		kseed @ 4 lit rot xkgen
		fka @ i 2 lit lshift + @ pins @ i 39 lit * + xkpub  orec @ 10 lit + pins @ i 39 lit * + 31 lit + 8 lit bcopy
		orec @ 18 lit + fps @ i 3 lit lshift + 8 lit bcopy
		orec @ 26 lit + c@ 8 lit u< 0= if 1 lit fbad ! then
		orec @ 25 lit + c@ orec @ 26 lit + c@ + 7 lit and  orec @ 27 lit + c@ if 8 lit + then  flv @ i 2 lit lshift + !
	loop
	\ the change output as made
	0 lit fchg !
	pend @ 4 lit + @ if
		pend @ 58 lit + pkb @ wpkof
		orec @ wknon  wmb @ wkmemo  pkb @ orec @ 10 lit + wmb @ onew @ wsmkout  onew @ fchg !
	then
	fbad @ if "an input has signed all it may" jerr else
	pins @ fnin @ pend @ 8 lit + pend @ 10 lit + fchg @ pend @ 18 lit + wsfin dup fcode !
	if fcode @ wfmsg else
		\ the leaves used, recorded before any signature
		wbeg
		fnin @ 0 lit do
			6F lit okey @ c!  pend @ 78 lit + i 5 lit lshift + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
			okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop
			orec @ 26 lit + c@ 1 lit + orec @ 26 lit + c!  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
		loop
		wend 0= if "the wallet could not be written" jerr else
			fka @ flv @ fps @ wstx ftx !
			"POST" "/v1/tx" wstxb @ ftx @ hask
			hcode @ C8 lit = if
				drop
				\ spent, the payment recorded (by its id: the body hash)
				wsd @ wsbody  wsd @ ecb @ wkcan
				wbeg
				fnin @ 0 lit do
					6F lit okey @ c!  pend @ 78 lit + i 5 lit lshift + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
					okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop  2 lit orec @ 24 lit + c!  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
				loop
				73 lit okey @ c!  wsa @ 8 lit + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  wtx @ okey @ 21 lit txdel drop
				orec @ 30 lit 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop drop
				pend @ 8 lit + orec @ 8 lit bcopy  pend @ 10 lit + orec @ 8 lit + 8 lit bcopy
				wsouts @ wschg @ 3C lit * + wsd @ wsocom  wsd @ orec @ 10 lit + wkcan
				70 lit okey @ c!  ecb @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
				wend drop
				jok ",'tx':'" jo ecb @ 20 lit jhex "','fee':'" jo pend @ 10 lit + a8. "'}" jo jend
			else
				?dup if "'reason':'" wtmp @ 100 lit jstr drop "the node refused it: " wtmp @ 100 lit + swap scpy wtmp @ scpy drop wtmp @ 100 lit + jerr
				else "the node is not reached" jerr then
			then
		then
	then then
then then then then then ;

\ hexs ( a n dst -- )  n bytes in hex, a string at dst.
: hxd  F lit and dup A lit u< if 30 lit + else 57 lit + then ;
: hexs
swap ?dup if 0 lit do over i + c@ dup 4 lit rshift hxd 2 lit pick c!  hxd over 1 lit + c!  2 lit + loop then
0 lit swap c!  drop ;
\ oact  the activity: payments sent (by their id; pending while the
\ node's pool holds them), outputs received (by their commitment).
: anum variable ;
: oact
have @ 0= if nowal else
	"/v1/mempool" hget wtmp @ !
	jok ",'items':[" jo  0 lit anum !
	wfd @ 0 lit txbegin wtx !
	70 lit okey @ c!  1 lit
	begin wtx @ okey @ rot okn @ txnext dup 21 lit = if okn @ c@ 70 lit = else 0 lit then  anum @ 10 lit u< and while
		drop  okn @ okey @ 21 lit bcopy  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop
		anum @ if "," jo then  anum @ 1 lit + anum !
		"{'tx':'" jo okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit jhex "','kind':'sent','amount':'" jo orec @ a8. "','state':'" jo
		okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit fout @ hexs
		wtmp @ @ ?dup if fout @ jfind else 0 lit then if "pending" else "confirmed" then jo "','height':0}" jo
		21 lit
	repeat drop
	6F lit okey @ c!  1 lit
	begin wtx @ okey @ rot okn @ txnext dup 21 lit = if okn @ c@ 6F lit = else 0 lit then  anum @ 10 lit u< and while
		drop  okn @ okey @ 21 lit bcopy  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop
		orec @ 29 lit + c@ 2 lit <> if
			anum @ if "," jo then  anum @ 1 lit + anum !
			"{'tx':'" jo okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit jhex "','kind':'received','amount':'" jo orec @ 10 lit + a8.
			"','state':'" jo orec @ 1C lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit = if "pending" else "confirmed" then jo
			"','height':" jo orec @ 20 lit + @ 0 lit wdec "}" jo
		then
		21 lit
	repeat drop
	wtx @ txabort drop
	"]}" jo jend
then ;

\ wsums  the balance in tabminer's five sums (wallet.rs's Balance), 8
\ bytes each: sa1 confirmed (unspent, in the set), sa2 pending (unspent,
\ not yet in it: change, rewards), sa4 unverified (an output added to
\ another's slate, not yet in the set), sa3 reserved (picked for a slate,
\ not signed), sa5 locked (signed away, still in the set).
: sa1 variable ;  : sa2 variable ;  : sa3 variable ;  : sa4 variable ;  : sa5 variable ;  : sacc variable ;
: a8z  0 lit over !  0 lit swap 4 lit + ! ;               \ ( a -- )
: wsums
sa1 @ a8z  sa2 @ a8z  sa3 @ a8z  sa4 @ a8z  sa5 @ a8z
wfd @ 0 lit txbegin wtx !
6F lit okey @ c!  1 lit
begin wtx @ okey @ rot okn @ txnext dup 21 lit = if okn @ c@ 6F lit = else 0 lit then while
	drop  okn @ okey @ 21 lit bcopy
	okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop
	0 lit sacc !
	orec @ 24 lit + c@ dup 0= if
		drop orec @ 1C lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit <> if sa1 else orec @ 29 lit + c@ 1 lit = if sa4 else sa2 then then @ sacc !
	else 1 lit = if sa3 @ sacc ! else
		orec @ 1C lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit <>  orec @ 28 lit + @ sgen @ = and if sa5 @ sacc ! then
	then then
	sacc @ if orec @ 10 lit + sacc @ sacc @ a8add then
	21 lit
repeat drop
wtx @ txabort drop ;

\ ── The requests ──

: tried variable ;
: oview
wtick  wsums
jok ",'confirmed':'" jo sa1 @ wsum.  "','pending':'" jo sa2 @ wsum.  "','unverified':'" jo sa4 @ wsum.  "','reserved':'" jo sa3 @ wsum.
"','locked':'" jo sa5 @ wsum.  "','height':" jo lh @ 0 lit wdec  ",'node':'" jo nodeok @ if "synced" else "not reached" then jo "'}" jo jend ;
\ oscan  the whole set scanned again now; the tip and the scan told.
: oscan
have @ 0= if nowal else
	jok "}" jo jend
	0 lit ltip @ c!  wtick
	"{'event':'scan','height':" jo lh @ 0 lit wdec ",'of':" jo lh @ 0 lit wdec "}" jo jend
then ;
: ocreate
have @ if "there is a wallet already" jerr else
	plain @ 10 lit wrand  plain @ wphr @ b39phr  wphr @ "" plain @ 10 lit + b39seed drop
	0 lit wmake if jok ",'words':'" jo wphr @ jraw "'}" jo jend  wtick else "the wallet could not be written" jerr then
then ;
: orestore
have @ if drop "there is a wallet already" jerr else
	dup "'words':'" wphr @ 100 lit jstr 0= if drop "no words" jerr else
		"'passphrase':'" wtmp @ 100 lit jstr drop
		wphr @ wtmp @ plain @ 10 lit + b39seed
		dup 0= if
			drop  wphr @ plain @ b39ent drop
			1 lit wmake if jok "}" jo jend  wtick else "the wallet could not be written" jerr then
		else
			dup FFFFFFFF lit = if drop "a phrase is 12 words" jerr else
			FFFFFFFE lit = if "a word is not in the list" jerr else
			"the checksum of the words does not match: a word is wrong" jerr then then
		then
	then
then ;
: ophrase
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
	"'password':'" wtmp @ 100 lit jstr 0= if "no password" jerr else
		wtmp @ wunseal if
			plain @ wphr @ b39phr  jok ",'words':'" jo wphr @ jraw "'}" jo jend
		else "not the password" jerr then
	then
then ;
: oreceive
have @ 0= if nowal else waddr!  jok ",'address':'" jo waddr @ jraw "'}" jo jend then ;

\ unlk ( line -- )  the first line: wm's, the session's password.
: unlk
"unlock" op? if
	"'password':'" pw @ 100 lit jstr pw @ c@ 0= 0= and if
		0 lit wopen if
			"secret" rec @ 100 lit wget 0< if
				1 lit unl !  "{'op':'unlock','ok':true,'wallet':false}" jo jend
			else
				pw @ wunseal if
					wload  1 lit unl !  "{'op':'unlock','ok':true,'wallet':true}" jo jend  wtick
				else "{'op':'unlock','ok':false,'error':'the wallet is sealed under another password than the session'}" jo jend then
			then
		else 1 lit unl !  "{'op':'unlock','ok':true,'wallet':false}" jo jend then
	else "{'op':'unlock','ok':false,'error':'no password'}" jo jend then
else drop "locked" jerr then ;

\ answer ( line -- )  a request answered by its op.
: answer
"overview" op? if drop have @ if oview else nowal then else
"receive" op? if drop oreceive else
"create" op? if drop ocreate else
"restore" op? if orestore else
"phrase" op? if ophrase else
"unlock" op? if drop "unlocked already" jerr else
"scan" op? if drop oscan else
"fees" op? if drop ofees else
"answer" op? if oanswer else
"send" op? if osend else
"finalize" op? if ofinal else
"activity" op? if drop oact else
"cancel" op? "bump" op? or if drop "not built yet" jerr else
drop "unknown op" jerr
then then then then then then then then then then then then then ;

\ hline ( line -- )  a line read: only the first may unlock.
: hline
dup getid  dup getop
unl @ if answer else tried @ if drop "locked" jerr else 1 lit tried ! unlk then then ;

\ lines  each whole line read handled; the rest, a line begun, kept.
: lines
0 lit lp !
begin
	lp @ le !
	begin le @ icnt @ u<  ibuf @ le @ + c@ A lit <> and while le @ 1 lit + le ! repeat
	le @ icnt @ u<
while
	0 lit ibuf @ le @ + c!  ibuf @ lp @ + hline
	le @ 1 lit + lp !
repeat
icnt @ lp @ - dup if dup 0 lit do ibuf @ lp @ + i + c@ ibuf @ i + c! loop then
icnt ! ;

wsinit  b39load drop  xkinit
1004 lit alloc ibuf !  1000 lit alloc obuf !  1000 lit alloc idb !  20 lit alloc opb !
100 lit alloc pw !  100 lit alloc rec !  60 lit alloc plain !  20 lit alloc wkey !  40 lit alloc salt2 !
100 lit alloc wphr !  1000 lit alloc wtmp !  8 lit alloc wcnt !  7A0 lit alloc wpk !  FC0 lit alloc wsk !  50 lit alloc waddr !
HMAX alloc hbuf !  200 lit alloc hreq !  100 lit alloc ppath !  20 lit alloc ntmp !
24 lit alloc okey !  24 lit alloc okn !  30 lit alloc orec !  20 lit alloc ecom !  14 lit alloc emem !  8 lit alloc eamt !
8 lit alloc epos !  4 lit alloc eh !  40 lit alloc ecb !  4 lit xksize alloc xk !  34 lit alloc wxpk !  20 lit alloc kseed !
8 lit alloc sfrom !  48 lit alloc ntip !  48 lit alloc ltip !  0 lit ltip @ c!  8 lit alloc sa1 !  8 lit alloc sa2 !  8 lit alloc sa3 !
8 lit alloc sa4 !  8 lit alloc sa5 !
0 lit lh !  0 lit nodeok !
FMAX alloc fbuf !  200 lit alloc fpath !  200 lit alloc fout !  40 lit alloc frk !  1000 lit alloc sel !
8 lit alloc samt !  8 lit alloc sfee !  8 lit alloc sneed !  8 lit alloc stot !  8 lit alloc schg !
8 lit alloc sdust !  5CDA lit 0 lit sdust @ a8set  880 lit alloc pend !  20 lit alloc sid !  20 lit alloc ssec !
20 lit alloc ssnd !  34 lit alloc pkb !  10 lit alloc nb !  14 lit alloc wmb !  40 lit alloc onew !
440 lit 40 lit * alloc fkeys !  100 lit alloc fka !  100 lit alloc flv !  200 lit alloc fps !  39 lit 40 lit * alloc pins !
: pfd variable ;  8 lit alloc pfd !  0 lit pfd @ !  1 lit pfd @ 4 lit + !
0 lit icnt !  0 lit unl !  0 lit tried !  0 lit have !  FFFFFFFF lit wfd !  obuf @ opos !
\ a line when one comes; the node every 4 s while none does
begin
	pfd @ 1 lit EE6B2800 lit poll 0 lit > if
		0 lit ibuf @ icnt @ + FFF lit icnt @ - read  dup 0 lit > if icnt @ + icnt !  lines  1 lit else drop 0 lit then
	else wtick 1 lit then
while repeat
bye
